{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting","id":1491335,"title":"Reach as an alternative to dice penalties when casting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-25T13:07:48-07:00","id":1491335,"title":"Reach as an alternative to dice penalties when casting?","content":"I'm considering this as a mechanics change in my Chronicle. Context: My players are extremely cautious. In the sessions we've had over the last several months, only one of them has risked Paradox during a single casting. That's how rarely they exceed free Reach. To mix things up, I'm considering letting them Reach for things like additional potency/duration rather than incurring penalties to their dice pool. So effectively, yes your chances of pulling off the spell aren't hindered, but your chances of Reaching beyond your safe range goes up in exchange for the extra oomph.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T13:24:36-07:00","id":1491337,"title":"","content":"Reach already does this? A Reach shifts a spell factor from basic to advanced, which is the difference between roughly one turn per point of duration or a near-exponential increase with a minimum of one scene or hour that reaches 24 hours at a single added point of duration.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that players who are cautious about risking Paradox is a problem in the first place, but if you want to add a little more tension around the issue, I would just suggest running them up against rival sorcerers who have no quandaries about their reach exceeding their grasp. Put the squeeze on them, make them feel like they <i>are</i> making a sacrifice being so cautious with their spellcraft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T14:17:30-07:00","id":1491347,"title":"","content":"Reach shifts into the advanced factors sure, but specifically with regard to potency, AFAIK the only way to increase it is by incurring a dice penalty.<br /> <br /> To your other point, I have been going a little too easy on them so they had time to find their sea legs. That's about to change though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:44:09-07:00","id":1491357,"title":"","content":"You can change the primary factor from duration to Potency, although I tend to houserule that you can change choose either since being stuck with the one you originally chose sounds odd when using such a flexible system.<br /> <br /> There are tons of ways to increase Potency. A simple example is casting a spell on oneself. Get a canteen of water, use a swiss army knife to drop the subject's blood into their reflection (+2 persona yantra), chant in High Speech (+2 mantra), spend ritual time purifying the caster with the water (+2 cleansing yantra) and draw a rune using a temporary tattoo marker (+2 rune yantra). If they have time for it, they can get a +1 bonus that does not count as a yantra with each extra interval taken, up to a +5. All those use widely available mundane components.<br /> <br /> Beyond that they need to either make items that work as specialized yantras (using Prime and Fate to enhance their bonus), utilize Willpower (or increase the bonus with a Perfecting of Mind), Fate boons, create perfected metal yantras, develop a Shadow Name or Cabal Theme, have a ephemeral being with an Influence compatible with the spell use an Enhance Influence when casting it to provide a dice bonus, overcome the Trials of Supernal Summons to gain a specialized tool (tattoo, a tool of its magical symbolism/tradition, etc) or quest beyond the material for them, and many more.<br /> <br /> Mages are at their best when they have time to prepare, the same goes for their tools. Sure, you can probably wear down an investigation site's Opacity, but its much easier if you use your lucky hag stone inscribed with runes that the Acanthus prepared or the magnifying sheets with Prime enhancements the Obrimos made, perhaps it adds just enough for them to benefit from an exceptional success. Even if they don't want to invest Willpower dots, they can make unsafely relinquished ones with enough duration to not go out of control, or they can trade favors with a crafter, requisition from their Order, etc. The more they invest in this, the more well defined each character's signature style will become.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I think <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1485150-storyteller-question-how-to-make-players-hubristics\">this thread</a> might prove useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-25-2022, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:13:12-07:00","id":1491362,"title":"","content":"I thought Yantra's only add to the dice pool and not Potency as the spell factor. I.E. If I cast an attack spell with Potency 2 and have a big dice pool from a bunch of Yantra's, success still deals only 2 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:14:22-07:00","id":1491363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting?p=1491357#post1491357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can change the primary factor from duration to Potency, although I tend to houserule that you can change choose either since being stuck with the one you originally chose sounds odd when using such a flexible system.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to Reach when changing the primary factor because primary factor is a ridiculously useful detail of the system. It is already such a big thing to get as many steps up it as your Arcanum rating by default, pushing it to the point of &quot;I can apply this to whichever factor would be the most useful in this circumstance with no cost whatsoever&quot; would make it actually broken. The fact that you are afforded the privilege of getting to change which factor it works with just for the cost of one Reach (which, I'll note, you can get several of which for free) is already the flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:34:16-07:00","id":1491369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shemihazazel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting?p=1491362#post1491362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Yantra's only add to the dice pool and not Potency as the spell factor. I.E. If I cast an attack spell with Potency 2 and have a big dice pool from a bunch of Yantra's, success still deals only 2 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can add to the dice pool, up to a bonus of +5 (which is detailed on page 112 of the core book). Anything beyond that is lost, which means its encouraged to use them for spell factors. Potency is one of those options, allowing the mage to take a -2 dice for each additional level of Potency (more information can be found on page 113 of the core book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-25-2022, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:38:07-07:00","id":1491370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting?p=1491363#post1491363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to Reach when changing the primary factor because primary factor is a ridiculously useful detail of the system. It is already such a big thing to get as many steps up it as your Arcanum rating by default, pushing it to the point of &quot;I can apply this to whichever factor would be the most useful in this circumstance with no cost whatsoever&quot; would make it actually broken. The fact that you are afforded the privilege of getting to change which factor it works with just for the cost of one Reach (which, I'll note, you can get several of which for free) is already the flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In most cases that makes sense, but some spells, such as <i>Impostor </i>and <i>Sleep of the Just</i>, are duration primary. Which means that, by default, they cannot affect anyone and will likely be withstood unless the caster takes several turns to build it up via yantras, making them not the most practical options when first unlocked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:08:09-07:00","id":1491372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting?p=1491370#post1491370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most cases that makes sense, but some spells, such as <i>Impostor </i>and <i>Sleep of the Just</i>, are duration primary. Which means that, by default, they cannot affect anyone and will likely be withstood unless the caster takes several turns to build it up via yantras, making them not the most practical options when first unlocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>The alternative being that you can make somebody stay awake or asleep or be perceived as somebody else for the whopping Duration of <i>one turn</i> without Reaching or adding factors, and in the event that you do bump those up, they do not have the insulation of having their Duration be the last factor to be reduced by Dissonance. <br /> <br /> Duration-primary spells are spells whose effects need to last more than they need to be able to overcome Withstand or provide a greater output. Potency-primary spells are typically the opposite. There is basically no spell that can be designed where one of those two things is not more important to the basic effect than its ability to affect a large number of people or a large area. Needing to take multiple turns to use Yantras is not an argument against this, because the default state of spellcasting takes at least ten minutes for the most powerful mages in the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T08:48:02-07:00","id":1491425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting?p=1491370#post1491370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless the caster takes several turns to build it up via yantras</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the game about sorcerers who harness occult symbols and correspondences to accomplish magical workings wants you to harness occult symbols and work at your magic rather than just point at a guy. Yantras aren't in the game for you to not use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T00:52:29-07:00","id":1491461,"title":"","content":"Also the mechanics are about choosing to risk small dice pool large spell factor spells (which either succeed with one success or fail completely) or less impressive spells which are more likely to succeed.<br /> <br /> Reach also gives you a trade off between safe free reach and paradox risk. But the paradox risk is fairly small given a) you can pay it down with mana, b) paradox success can be absorbed as bashing damage (15 minutes to heal, which is considerably less than the ritual casting time you might be using without the reach), c) paradox conditions aren't actually bad - they mostly make it more likely to gain more paradox, which is a paradox spiral, but you can just keep containing the paradox until your character sheet is filled with bashing and you collapse from the pain (you get to roll to avoid collapsing, but this looks great from a narrative point of view, low wisdom mages can essentially contain and ignore paradox conditions all day long...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shemihazazel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting#post1491335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm considering this as a mechanics change in my Chronicle. Context: My players are extremely cautious. In the sessions we've had over the last several months, only one of them has risked Paradox during a single casting. That's how rarely they exceed free Reach. To mix things up, I'm considering letting them Reach for things like additional potency/duration rather than incurring penalties to their dice pool. So effectively, yes your chances of pulling off the spell aren't hindered, but your chances of Reaching beyond your safe range goes up in exchange for the extra oomph.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a problem? They have these two choices/risks. Reach vs paradox risk, and dice pool vs spell factors (risk of failing to cast). You could ally them with an NPC who is Gnosis 1 and forced to overreach to cast effective spells, but who manages to contain the paradox most of the time. Just to demonstrate how it is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T05:04:31-07:00","id":1491583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491335-reach-as-an-alternative-to-dice-penalties-when-casting?p=1491370#post1491370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most cases that makes sense, but some spells, such as <i>Impostor </i>and <i>Sleep of the Just</i>, are duration primary. Which means that, by default, they cannot affect anyone and will likely be withstood unless the caster takes several turns to build it up via yantras, making them not the most practical options when first unlocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think citing one of the circumstances in which somebody would like to switch primary factors with no cost whatsoever is itself a very compelling argument that &quot;I can apply this to whichever factor would be most useful in this circumstance with no cost whatsoever&quot; would <i>not</i> make it actually broken.<br /> <br /> Like, the whole premise of Withstand is that sometimes you have to go the extra mile to make a spell take hold, which is the case even if Potency is primary for a spell. I'm not really moved by a person saying that they don't want to go the extra mile, so they'd like the option to skip all or most of the line on every occasion rather than just lots or most occasions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}